Third-party software shipped in the built application.

Each entry gives the component, the version shipped, its licence and where its
source is available. The WebAssembly engines are copied unmodified from the npm
packages pinned in package-lock.json (see scripts/vendor-wasm.mjs) and are
served from wasm/<engine>-<version>/ in the build, next to the licence and
notice files their packages ship. The corresponding source for each binary is
the named release of the project that built it, whose build scripts pin the
exact versions of the libraries listed under it. This file and the app's own
licence are also in the build as THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt and LICENSE.txt.

